    "field": "Paleoclimate reconstruction",
    "problem": "Reconstructing Holocene global temperature has been challenging due to limited proxy data and methodological uncertainties, preventing a robust assessment of past climate variability and the discrepancy between proxy evidence and climate models.",
    "method": "This study proposes a multi-method approach that applies five different statistical methods to an extensive new multi-proxy database to reconstruct Holocene global mean surface temperature, aggregating the results into an ensemble to provide a realistic range of uncertainties.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct the global mean surface temperature for the past 12,000 years by applying five different statistical methods to a new multi-proxy database, creating a robust multi-method ensemble that accounts for various uncertainties.",
